o to move on  well certainly we spent two and a half  years just listening to patients  listening to their families  listening to  uh the tremendous traumas that they'd  been through and it was  really tragic that women who had had  mesh  lost their jobs because they were too  ill to work because they lost their job  they then couldn't pay the mortgage  because they couldn't pay the mortgage  they then were homeless because they  they were homeless there was a real risk  that their children would be taken into  care  so it was  downward spiral and the suffering that  we witnessed i will take to my grave it  was simply appalling the huge effects  that it had and of course some of the  people had actually died well veronica  campbell as you continue to fight on  their behalf and thank you for speaking  up for those victims today  we appreciate your time here on sky news  thank you very much
 

